From 2de0a3a4e873d537013a92ef44512fe445fbf8f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:48:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the LLM provider layer for Ditto on the official
 anthropic and openai SDKs

orchestrator/llm replaces LiteLLM for Ditto (not wired in yet; nothing imports
litellm here):

- types/errors: provider-neutral messages, tools, requests and results with the
  provider's own assistant turn kept for append-only histories; user-facing
  errors mapped from both SDKs (keys redacted), incl. billing/quota errors.
- anthropic: Messages API without sampling parameters or thinking config,
  explicit output_config.effort, tool_choice auto with strict closed schemas,
  output_config.format for JSON answers, automatic prompt caching (5m/1h),
  server-side refusal fallback (fallbacks "default") for Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5
  and Fable 5.1 on the Claude API, Refused on stop_reason refusal, API key or
  an `ant auth login` OAuth profile read by the SDK; never the environment.
- openai_compat: Chat Completions for llama-server, Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio,
  OpenRouter and Gemini's OpenAI endpoint; response_format json_schema, effort
  only where the server understands it, no tools+response_format for
  llama-server, org/project/env never leak to third-party servers.
- openai_responses: OpenAI's own models (tool calling only there), store=false
  with output items replayed unchanged, per-install prompt_cache_key.
- claude_code: the user's Claude subscription through their own, unmodified
  Claude Code (`claude -p`), signed in with Claude Code's own login; no token
  is ever read or stored by the framework (Anthropic's terms forbid that).
- catalog + configs/llm_providers.yml: presets as data, model per task
  profile, free-text and live model lists for unknown models.
- privacy: STRICT/BALANCED/OFF filter for cloud providers with HMAC-stable
  placeholders (cache-friendly) and local restoration of answers.
- client: provider/model per task from the settings, retries for 429/5xx
  honouring Retry-After (SDK retries off), fallback chain on refusals and
  outages; run_tool_loop keeps tools identical and the history append-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
